{
 "_doc": "Per model: category (folder under /Game/Free); size = what the real thing measures along its largest side in metres (the file is rescaled only when it is off by more than a quarter, a unit mistake); scale = a fixed factor instead (packs, where no one size fits); split = a pack of separate props (one asset per prop); keep / drop = mesh node names to keep or leave out (the C10 comes on a diorama with a road, poles and cacti); nanite = force Nanite on or off (default: on from 50k triangles when no material is translucent). Poly Haven models are scanned at their real size and keep it. own = a .glb of Tom's own in ~/Assets/signal47-free/own (no credit); pivot model = a split model's props keep the whole model's pivot (the printer's paper stays in place). repaint = a function in repaint.py run on the model's textures (the sheriff's livery; brand logos painted out); full_uv = UVs kept at full precision (a building's tiling textures in metres); trim = the exported building it replaces cut out of the town's merged meshes (trim_web.py: the group, the materials to keep, boxes in the group's metres x0 x1 y0 y1 z0 z1); cuts = the triangles of the named meshes inside a box (metres in the prepared model: x forward, y up, pivot at the middle of the base) made an asset of their own, <model>_<cut>, with the model's pivot (the patrol car's driver's door, which opens).",
